WEBVTT

00:00:07.750 --> 00:00:08.710
Yuito.

00:00:08.710 --> 00:00:11.510
Yeah, he's forced our hand!

00:01:08.360 --> 00:01:10.400
Karen!

00:01:10.400 --> 00:01:12.860
Out of my way, Fubuki.

00:01:16.780 --> 00:01:19.870
Karen. Stop this madness.

00:01:19.870 --> 00:01:23.290
I didn't realize the depths
of your suffering.

00:01:23.290 --> 00:01:24.620
Shut it.

00:01:24.620 --> 00:01:27.960
Stop this. You've done more
than enough already.

00:01:27.960 --> 00:01:29.500
I...

00:01:29.500 --> 00:01:34.960
I don't want to see you suffer like this,
and neither would Alice.

00:01:34.960 --> 00:01:36.340
Shut it!

00:01:36.340 --> 00:01:37.800
Karen!

00:01:37.800 --> 00:01:41.140
We must live here and now in this world!

00:01:41.140 --> 00:01:44.390
We must live in a world without Alice!

00:01:47.310 --> 00:01:51.060
I understand how you feel.

00:01:51.060 --> 00:01:53.980
But we must accept that she's gone.

00:01:53.980 --> 00:01:58.360
Let's live... Let's live here
in the present.

00:02:03.490 --> 00:02:08.000
Karen, please. We need your help.

00:02:08.000 --> 00:02:13.040
We need you to go to the Chronos Terminal
and unravel the entanglements you caused.

00:02:13.040 --> 00:02:17.340
I don't want to shut
the door on the future.

00:02:17.340 --> 00:02:19.840
We won't let you do this.

00:02:19.840 --> 00:02:22.140
End this here and now...

00:02:22.140 --> 00:02:25.850
...for your own sake and
all those who hold you dear.

00:02:28.480 --> 00:02:30.690
I see.

00:02:30.690 --> 00:02:34.270
This is as far as I get.

00:02:34.270 --> 00:02:36.320
Then...

00:02:36.320 --> 00:02:40.610
it seems that, too, is another choice.

00:02:48.410 --> 00:02:49.750
Yuito.

00:04:27.260 --> 00:04:32.270
"Operation Destroy the Kunad Gate"

00:04:37.190 --> 00:04:37.900
"Warning"

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.730
"Warning"

00:04:37.900 --> 00:04:40.730
Hey! What are you seeing on your screen?!

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:43.740
"Warning"

00:04:40.730 --> 00:04:43.740
No good here, either.
Too much data to process!

00:04:43.740 --> 00:04:47.950
The growth rate is off the charts.
If this keeps up...

00:04:47.950 --> 00:04:50.700
It's exceeding the measurable limit.

00:04:51.540 --> 00:04:52.410
It's no use!

00:04:52.410 --> 00:04:53.250
Damnit!

00:04:53.250 --> 00:04:54.080
What's happening?!

00:04:54.080 --> 00:04:56.170
It got cut off!

00:04:56.170 --> 00:04:57.210
The system...!

00:04:57.210 --> 00:04:58.920
I'm shutting it down!

00:05:04.470 --> 00:05:05.380
"Warning: System Shutdown"

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:10.970
"Warning: System Shutdown"

00:05:05.380 --> 00:05:10.970
There's nothing more we can do.

00:05:10.970 --> 00:05:12.970
"System Shutdown"

00:05:43.300 --> 00:05:44.840
Good morning.

00:05:46.010 --> 00:05:48.550
Fubuki.

00:05:48.550 --> 00:05:53.220
Is this where the regiment
commander should be right now?

00:05:53.220 --> 00:05:56.690
We may have lucked out for once.

00:05:56.690 --> 00:06:00.400
The Others have gone eerily silent.

00:06:01.820 --> 00:06:06.150
I wonder if they fear
the same thing we do.

00:06:08.280 --> 00:06:12.200
Alice once told me something.

00:06:12.200 --> 00:06:14.700
She said, "I wish Karen smiled more."

00:06:14.700 --> 00:06:18.830
"He doesn't look bad with a smile."

00:06:18.830 --> 00:06:22.380
I haven't seen you smile since that day.

00:06:22.380 --> 00:06:26.550
Then again, that was a rare
sight to begin with.

00:06:29.550 --> 00:06:33.260
I doubt I can heal
the pain you feel inside.

00:06:33.260 --> 00:06:36.890
But I won't give up hope.

00:06:36.890 --> 00:06:40.100
I hope you can live your life

00:06:40.100 --> 00:06:45.070
and that you will once again
be able to smile someday

00:06:45.070 --> 00:06:47.030
right here in this world.

00:06:49.450 --> 00:06:52.280
All you want me to do is
unravel my entanglements

00:06:52.280 --> 00:06:54.200
so that the Kunad Gate disappears?

00:06:54.200 --> 00:06:55.540
Huh?

00:06:55.540 --> 00:07:00.670
Fubuki, surely you've realized
what else is possible.

00:07:07.510 --> 00:07:09.420
Major General Fubuki.

00:07:09.420 --> 00:07:12.180
You finally came to.

00:07:12.180 --> 00:07:13.640
Karen.

00:07:16.640 --> 00:07:20.850
We'll need your help to
carry out the operation.

00:07:20.850 --> 00:07:23.100
Think you're up to it?

00:07:23.100 --> 00:07:24.610
An operation?

00:07:24.610 --> 00:07:28.280
Why were you opposing me this whole time?

00:07:28.280 --> 00:07:29.860
The Kunad Gate?

00:07:29.860 --> 00:07:32.950
Yes, but there's more than that.

00:07:32.950 --> 00:07:35.740
We'll also destroy the Extinction Belt.

00:07:35.740 --> 00:07:37.830
Destroy the Extinction Belt?

00:07:37.830 --> 00:07:41.710
Your brother, Kaito, drafted a plan
to have the Kunad Gate

00:07:41.710 --> 00:07:43.790
consume the Extinction Belt.

00:07:43.790 --> 00:07:46.800
That's right. But it won't work.

00:07:46.800 --> 00:07:49.840
Even with Kasane and my gravikinesis,

00:07:49.840 --> 00:07:51.760
we'd still be underpowered.

00:07:51.760 --> 00:07:53.050
Don't tell me...!

00:07:54.140 --> 00:07:59.100
We already tried amplifying our power
by connecting all the nation's brains.

00:07:59.100 --> 00:08:03.650
So this time, we'll try using Arahabaki
with our power alone.

00:08:03.650 --> 00:08:06.360
The city's network capabilities
are paralyzed,

00:08:06.360 --> 00:08:08.690
but Arahabaki itself still functions.

00:08:08.690 --> 00:08:13.570
If we connect via SAS,
we can boost our psionic power.

00:08:13.570 --> 00:08:16.780
Arahabaki has conducted
every possible simulation

00:08:16.780 --> 00:08:18.540
over several hundred years.

00:08:18.540 --> 00:08:20.250
Is that even possible?

00:08:20.250 --> 00:08:23.670
There's just one problem.

00:08:23.670 --> 00:08:26.790
We don't know if your and Kasane's brains

00:08:26.790 --> 00:08:30.050
can withstand the power
of Arahabaki's amplified output.

00:08:31.760 --> 00:08:34.380
Even if there's only a small chance,

00:08:34.380 --> 00:08:36.890
we have to try.

00:08:36.890 --> 00:08:38.680
It's settled, then.

00:08:40.600 --> 00:08:45.020
You'll destroy the Kunad Gate and
Extinction Belt in one fell swoop?

00:08:45.020 --> 00:08:48.940
Countless lives will be saved if it works.

00:08:48.940 --> 00:08:52.490
No! Yuito's body has
already reached its limit!

00:08:52.490 --> 00:08:55.320
What'll happen if you
push him even harder?

00:08:55.320 --> 00:08:57.490
You all agree, don't you?

00:09:02.250 --> 00:09:06.170
Hanabi's right.
Yuito shouldn't be a part of this.

00:09:06.170 --> 00:09:11.920
Even if we connect to Arahabaki
to amplify our power,

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:17.010
do you think Kasane and Karen alone will
be enough to move the Extinction Belt?

00:09:17.010 --> 00:09:22.180
Honestly, I find it far-fetched that
anything could move something so massive.

00:09:22.180 --> 00:09:25.270
It's better to see it as our
one and only chance.

00:09:25.270 --> 00:09:28.400
We've gotta hit it with all we've got.

00:09:28.400 --> 00:09:31.190
The time for caution is long past.

00:09:32.280 --> 00:09:34.780
Yeah, but...

00:09:34.780 --> 00:09:36.740
Yuito.

00:09:36.740 --> 00:09:39.200
Sorry to keep you waiting.

00:09:39.200 --> 00:09:40.990
Yuito!

00:09:40.990 --> 00:09:45.330
You look terrible.
You really need to rest!

00:09:45.330 --> 00:09:47.500
No need to worry about me.

00:09:47.500 --> 00:09:51.840
What are you talking about?!
You can barely stay on your feet!

00:09:51.840 --> 00:09:54.300
I have to do this.

00:09:54.300 --> 00:09:57.300
You'll all support me via SAS, right?

00:09:57.300 --> 00:09:59.140
Everything will be okay.

00:10:02.350 --> 00:10:04.430
Do you have a death wish?

00:10:04.430 --> 00:10:05.640
What?

00:10:05.640 --> 00:10:08.650
You're always pushing yourself too hard.

00:10:08.650 --> 00:10:12.520
You think your death will
solve everything, don't you?

00:10:12.520 --> 00:10:13.980
Don't be stupid!

00:10:13.980 --> 00:10:18.030
What do you think we've been
fighting for this whole time?!

00:10:18.030 --> 00:10:19.660
For you.

00:10:19.660 --> 00:10:24.120
But no matter what we say, I bet
you'll take part in the operation.

00:10:24.120 --> 00:10:25.330
Sorry.

00:10:27.710 --> 00:10:30.630
There's but one thing we must do.

00:10:30.630 --> 00:10:32.750
No matter how reckless Yuito is...

00:10:32.750 --> 00:10:35.210
...we must make sure he lives.

00:10:38.510 --> 00:10:39.760
Hanabi.

00:10:46.930 --> 00:10:48.230
Thank you.

00:10:48.230 --> 00:10:49.600
Hanabi...

00:10:53.940 --> 00:10:58.610
The Suoh OSF has taken defensive positions
along with the Seiran Regional Force.

00:10:58.610 --> 00:11:01.910
Roger that. Standby for further commands.

00:11:01.910 --> 00:11:02.950
Yes, sir.

00:11:05.990 --> 00:11:08.200
Let me make this clear.

00:11:08.200 --> 00:11:10.500
I let you copy my power out of necessity.

00:11:10.500 --> 00:11:12.290
But if you try anything funny--

00:11:12.290 --> 00:11:17.050
Don't worry. I will give you
what you want.

00:11:17.050 --> 00:11:18.590
Karen.

00:11:20.010 --> 00:11:22.300
You doubt me, too, little brother?

00:11:22.300 --> 00:11:25.220
That's not what I was going to say.

00:11:25.220 --> 00:11:28.930
Relax. I'm going to make sure this works.

00:11:28.930 --> 00:11:31.390
I'll hold you to that.

00:11:31.390 --> 00:11:33.440
Are we good to go?

00:11:33.440 --> 00:11:35.520
Connection to Arahabaki complete.

00:11:35.520 --> 00:11:37.440
Ready when you are!

00:11:37.440 --> 00:11:40.950
This time, we'll help, too,
by connecting with SAS!

00:11:40.950 --> 00:11:43.620
Kasane, Yuito.
Let's give it our best shot!

00:11:43.620 --> 00:11:45.030
--Okay!
--Okay!

00:11:45.030 --> 00:11:49.000
I know this is a heavy lift for you all,
but we appreciate the help.

00:11:49.000 --> 00:11:50.540
We're gonna make this work!

00:11:50.540 --> 00:11:52.580
I know we can do this.

00:11:52.580 --> 00:11:56.500
After all, we've been
through so much together.

00:11:56.500 --> 00:11:59.010
Okay, let's do this!

00:12:05.390 --> 00:12:09.350
Arahabaki, commence SAS connection!

00:12:23.200 --> 00:12:24.860
What is this?!

00:12:28.950 --> 00:12:30.700
"Kasane" "Yuito"

00:12:30.950 --> 00:12:34.040
Suoh OSF, Seiran Regional Force,

00:12:34.040 --> 00:12:38.380
the Others went quiet, but who
knows when they will strike again?!

00:12:38.380 --> 00:12:41.510
All we can do now is
protect the operation team.

00:12:41.510 --> 00:12:45.930
That's what we, the defenders of New
Himuka, can do for the planet.

00:12:45.930 --> 00:12:49.260
Do not let a single Other get past you!

00:12:49.260 --> 00:12:50.560
Yes, sir!

00:12:53.230 --> 00:12:55.730
We'll start with the Extinction Belt!

00:12:55.730 --> 00:12:56.900
Okay!

00:13:17.170 --> 00:13:19.960
No reaction from the Extinction Belt yet.

00:13:19.960 --> 00:13:22.760
The connection with Arahabaki is unstable!

00:13:22.760 --> 00:13:25.550
Yuito! Kasane! You gotta focus!

00:13:25.550 --> 00:13:27.680
We know!

00:13:27.680 --> 00:13:30.310
If we don't control this power...!

00:13:32.310 --> 00:13:35.520
Move, damn you!

00:13:40.190 --> 00:13:42.440
The Belt's starting to move!

00:13:42.440 --> 00:13:47.240
But if we let our minds drift even a bit,
we'll black out!

00:13:47.240 --> 00:13:50.530
We can't give up--no matter what!

00:13:58.250 --> 00:14:01.630
Leave the control of Arahabaki to me.

00:14:01.630 --> 00:14:05.170
I was connected for 2,000 years.
I can handle it.

00:14:06.630 --> 00:14:07.680
Karen.

00:14:07.680 --> 00:14:08.930
Do it!

00:14:20.480 --> 00:14:21.310
Kasane!

00:14:21.310 --> 00:14:22.570
Ready!

00:14:36.960 --> 00:14:39.170
The Extinction Belt is...

00:14:40.580 --> 00:14:42.460
It's really working?

00:14:45.340 --> 00:14:50.300
Yes! The Kunad Gate is
devouring the Extinction Belt!

00:14:50.300 --> 00:14:51.510
Wow.

00:14:51.510 --> 00:14:53.600
Good riddance!

00:14:56.430 --> 00:14:58.640
It might actually work.

00:14:58.640 --> 00:15:00.230
Looking good.

00:15:03.770 --> 00:15:05.440
Yuito.

00:15:09.280 --> 00:15:10.990
Yuito!

00:15:10.990 --> 00:15:11.870
Oh, no!

00:15:11.870 --> 00:15:13.620
The Belt is...!

00:15:23.130 --> 00:15:25.210
This is bad!

00:15:35.430 --> 00:15:37.140
Hold the line!

00:15:37.140 --> 00:15:39.140
Prepare to intercept!

00:15:40.600 --> 00:15:42.150
Yuito!

00:16:14.090 --> 00:16:15.800
Yuito.

00:16:15.800 --> 00:16:17.100
Yuito?

00:16:17.100 --> 00:16:18.310
Yuito!

00:16:18.310 --> 00:16:19.640
Yuito!

00:16:21.230 --> 00:16:23.350
Sorry. I...

00:16:23.350 --> 00:16:25.360
That's all right. You still good?

00:16:25.360 --> 00:16:26.650
Yeah!

00:16:28.270 --> 00:16:30.150
This is it!

00:16:30.150 --> 00:16:32.200
Give it everything you've got!

00:16:32.200 --> 00:16:34.160
Hang in there, Yuito!

00:16:34.160 --> 00:16:37.330
Harness our power!

00:16:39.240 --> 00:16:42.250
You said you could save the world.

00:16:42.250 --> 00:16:44.670
Now it's time to prove it!

00:16:48.130 --> 00:16:53.760
For the future!

00:17:04.440 --> 00:17:05.940
Damn it.

00:17:25.670 --> 00:17:28.590
The Extinction Belt is gone.

00:17:28.590 --> 00:17:31.340
It's too soon to celebrate.

00:17:31.340 --> 00:17:35.840
We have to go to the Chronos Terminal
and unravel the remaining entanglements.

00:17:35.840 --> 00:17:36.930
Right.

00:17:36.930 --> 00:17:39.550
There's no need for that.

00:17:41.930 --> 00:17:42.770
Karen!

00:17:42.770 --> 00:17:44.600
Don't!

00:17:44.600 --> 00:17:48.270
It turns out I can't give up hope.

00:17:48.270 --> 00:17:49.900
What are you doing?!

00:17:49.900 --> 00:17:51.360
D-Don't!

00:17:51.360 --> 00:17:52.610
Wait!

00:17:52.610 --> 00:17:56.030
Did I not tell you
I'd give you what you want?

00:17:56.030 --> 00:18:00.160
I've no intention of becoming
Yakumo anymore.

00:18:03.870 --> 00:18:07.750
This is my final trip back.

00:18:08.630 --> 00:18:09.750
Don't do it.

00:18:09.750 --> 00:18:11.340
Karen.

00:18:17.380 --> 00:18:19.220
He's gone.

00:19:09.350 --> 00:19:13.060
The system is picking up Red Strings
readings all across Suoh!

00:19:13.060 --> 00:19:16.440
It's happening in Seiran
and Togetsu as well!

00:19:16.440 --> 00:19:20.160
It must be an incredibly
widespread phenomenon.

00:19:20.160 --> 00:19:22.120
What is happening?

00:19:26.830 --> 00:19:29.000
Yuito, look!

00:19:36.880 --> 00:19:39.260
The Kunad Gate is...

00:19:43.470 --> 00:19:45.600
It's beautiful.

00:19:45.600 --> 00:19:49.020
Did we actually pull it off?

00:19:54.980 --> 00:19:56.940
--They did it.
--How wonderful!

00:19:56.940 --> 00:20:00.400
The sky is... so blue.

00:20:15.590 --> 00:20:17.210
Karen...

00:20:17.210 --> 00:20:21.720
Those red lines we just saw.
Was that Red Strings' power?

00:20:21.720 --> 00:20:27.640
I wonder if the world was somehow
affected by Karen traveling to the past.

00:20:27.640 --> 00:20:30.980
You mean besides the Kunad Gate
being destroyed?

00:20:32.770 --> 00:20:34.810
That had me totally captivated.

00:20:34.810 --> 00:20:36.900
Now to look into what happened!

00:20:36.900 --> 00:20:38.270
Let's do this, Haruka!

00:20:38.270 --> 00:20:41.400
Way ahead of you, big brother!

00:20:43.860 --> 00:20:46.120
Someone was looking out for us.

00:20:47.950 --> 00:20:50.540
We did more than save the future.

00:20:52.040 --> 00:20:54.960
We also destroyed the Extinction Belt.

00:20:54.960 --> 00:20:59.420
And we did it together with Karen.

00:20:59.420 --> 00:21:01.340
Yeah.

00:21:01.340 --> 00:21:04.300
We've forged a new future.

00:21:09.010 --> 00:21:14.310
Karen, wherever you are,
are you gazing up at this same sky?

00:21:17.810 --> 00:21:19.480
We did it!

00:21:30.990 --> 00:21:38.840
<i>I've been a prisoner</i>
<i>of my own longing</i>

00:21:40.630 --> 00:21:48.430
<i>The shimmering heat signals me to halt</i>

00:21:48.430 --> 00:21:50.560
<i>There's a stranger in me</i>

00:21:50.560 --> 00:21:53.060
<i>I'll fly high so I won't be scared</i>

00:21:53.060 --> 00:21:58.310
<i>By this new self I've never seen</i>

00:21:58.310 --> 00:22:00.070
<i>I'm spreading my wings</i>

00:22:00.070 --> 00:22:02.440
<i>Bird in florid flight</i>

00:22:02.440 --> 00:22:07.160
<i>Lift your eyes to the scarlet sky</i>

00:22:07.160 --> 00:22:12.370
<i>Overtaken by the mighty wind</i>

00:22:12.370 --> 00:22:17.540
<i>The view unfolds upon a world</i>
<i>that begins turning</i>

00:22:17.540 --> 00:22:22.000
<i>Amid the intermingling light</i>

00:22:22.000 --> 00:22:27.880
<i>I keep searching for tomorrow</i>

00:22:27.880 --> 00:22:29.510
<i>Tomorrow's in your hands</i>

00:22:29.510 --> 00:22:32.720
<i>Don't tell me now you're afraid</i>

00:22:32.720 --> 00:22:34.350
<i>There's no time to waste</i>

00:22:34.350 --> 00:22:37.310
<i>Keep going forward</i>

00:22:37.310 --> 00:22:41.650
<i>There's nothing to be afraid of</i>

00:22:41.650 --> 00:22:43.320
<i>Now, let's go</i>

00:22:43.320 --> 00:22:48.780
<i>Into a brand-new day</i>

00:22:54.040 --> 00:22:55.830
"Search Results"

00:22:55.830 --> 00:22:57.250
What could this mean?

00:22:57.250 --> 00:23:00.130
There's no data on Karen anywhere.

00:23:00.130 --> 00:23:01.080
Huh?

00:23:01.080 --> 00:23:03.090
It's true. I've quadruple checked.

00:23:03.090 --> 00:23:05.760
Major General Fubuki!

00:23:05.760 --> 00:23:09.720
It seems the operation was a success!

00:23:09.720 --> 00:23:11.300
So it seems.

00:23:14.680 --> 00:23:17.270
We did it, Fubuki!

00:23:17.270 --> 00:23:19.640
A-Alice?

00:23:21.520 --> 00:23:24.070
What's wrong? Why do you look so shocked?

00:23:24.070 --> 00:23:26.400
No, it's just...

00:23:27.780 --> 00:23:31.610
Hanabi. I'm glad to see you're safe.

00:23:31.610 --> 00:23:33.910
Y-Yeah...

00:23:35.490 --> 00:23:38.580
Alice, you're...

00:23:38.580 --> 00:23:44.210
It's just, there's something
I need to ask you.

00:23:44.210 --> 00:23:48.300
It's about... Karen.

00:23:50.760 --> 00:23:52.260
Fubuki.

00:23:52.260 --> 00:23:55.850
Who's Karen?

00:24:09.150 --> 00:24:11.910
"To Each Their Own Future"
